A||||25||GT Bastard||Raced a twin-turbo RX7 and a V-Tec Prelude||||1||
Z||000000||GT Bastard||03-23-2001||01:35 AM||||Hope I'm not boring anyone with race stories, but this one was interesting.  I came across a very clean newish V-Tec(yes, a real Vtec car) Prelude that was lowered with custom wheels and an aftermarket exhaust.  We played around a little bit, and then his buddy eventually joins in with a '93 RX7(new bodied, factory twins.)  The RX7 pulls along side and I say "nice car."  He responds with, "wanna see what it's got?"  I told him allright, but I already knew I'd lose.  His car sounded downright EVIL.  It's got an HKS sequential blow-off valve, an exhaust, and god knows what else.  Anyhow, we agree to race near an industial park.  Nice flat road for about 2 miles.... We launch on the count of three.  My SE chirps the tires sticks really well off the line, His car barks the tires as well, but he didn't spin.  Much to my surprise I pulled an easy 2 car-lengths off the launch!  I slammed it into second gear and he's on my rear bumper.  1/2 way through second gear he starts pulling away pretty quickly.  By about 80mph, he's handed me my a$$ on a platter.  Afterwords, he says, "did you hit the button?"  I grinned like an idiot and said, "I haven't got nitrous."  I couldn't believe I jumped him off the line!  Then his buddy pulls up in the prelude and said he said something about the launch being good(I was plum full of adrenaline, and don't remember exactly.)  The V-Tec Prelude asks if I want to run, and I said sure.  Blah blah blah, we launch.  He spins the hell outta his tires and I launched. By the time he got traction, I had an easy 6 or 7 car-lengths.  It pretty much stayed that way the rest of the race, so acceleration was pretty evenly matched.  We chatted a while afterwords, and they seemed pretty cool.  The Honda driver seemed really surprised(especially after I let him hear my engine rattle), but he was cool about it.  He wanted to race again on the way back... This time I took him off the line again, but I missed second!  Oh well, I was still really pleased with the previous races.  I'm psyched to get my engine finished so that I can juice-it again.  whew....<P><BR>ps-I should mention that this isn't the same car that I killed the civic in, that was my basically stock GT.  The SE is modded...<BR>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/gtbastard.gif">      <P>"My heroes are John Wayne, the Simpsons, and whoever canceled Full House/Bob Saget."<p>[This message has been edited by GT Bastard (edited 03-23-2001).]||||reg||1
