Z||000010||AkursedX||03-23-2001||03:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GT Bastard:<BR><B><P>4-puck ACT clutch<BR>Chris West headers(although they didn't really gain anything on the dyno)<BR>Custom 2.5 exhaust, no cat, flowmaster<BR>fuel system and computer related changes(diff prom)<BR>4.10, 4sp tranny<BR>Furby<BR>MSD ingnition<BR>modified intake<BR>larger TB<BR>Extrude honed intake<BR>Si valves and stiffer springs<BR>I know I'm missing stuff<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>I HAVE THE FURBY MOD TOO!!!!!!  I swear the thing gives me at least 15 more hp!!  I also have custom smurf and lobster mods as well!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Voytek||03-23-2001||06:00 PM||||That's impressive.  As long as we're on the topic - last summer I was in a small town in British Columbia.  Cruisin down a back road about 60 km (38 mph) I had a Porsche 944 pull up on my a$$ and going in and out of his lane like he's in a hurry somewhere.  As we turn into a side road, before I realized it, he takes me.  I was at a loss from there but we got it up to about 90 mph in a 35 mph zone.  I stopped at my campground and he kept on.  5 minutes later he comes around and asks if I want to race.  My '87 GT bumblebee doesn't mind so I said yes.  As I found out it was an '87 944 (with the wide wheel arches - looked like a nice shape).  So we found a road by a little airport.  We lined up on it once the traffic died down (he was very confident - he decided to go against the traffic).  First try: by the second gear I was about 2 car lengths ahead and stayed that way.  He seemed to have lost a bit of traction off the line, so as he pulled up next to me, I gave him another opportunity to prove his manhood.  Second try: no spinning - my car? At least 1.5 car lengths ahead by second gear and stayed that way up to 90 mph.  All I can say is AMERICAN TORQUE RULES!  GTBastard - that's probably what helped you with the RX7.||||reg||1
Z||000012||stsmithgt||03-23-2001||06:43 PM||||Hmmmmmmm.  I put about 5 yrs. working at a Mazda dealership.  With a twin turbo to take advantage of, that guy sounds like he had the money to fix up his car, but not the know how or desire to race it hard(thrash it).  No offence intended because it sounded like too much fun to down anyone, just my ¢².  Those RX-7's I drove were rockets if you kept there RPM's up in its power band and with turbo's geez.  We use to fight over the turbo's that came into the shop, never twins though, <I>(new cars not customers....yet.)</I>to see who got to test drive the sucker. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  That was gravy money to inspect those cars.  Our assistant manager of the dealership <I>(owners son..)</I>took the very first RX-7 the dealership got and totaled it the same day. HAH!  He missed a curve.  Somehow he hit a road sign six feet off the ground.  I guess they fly too.  (when you drive into ditch and launch back out) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Did I use enough brackets?()[]()[]()||||reg||5
Z||000013||danny boy||03-23-2001||07:09 PM||||I like hearing (rice)race stories. Gotta love that Fiero torque. The RX7 has (I think) a 1.3L rotary motor. Ain't got nuthin til them turbos spool.  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/stealth_feb2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000014||GT Bastard||03-23-2001||07:20 PM||||I think the key factors were: Fiero=sticky launch with plenty of torque. RX7=Turbo lag, and I doubt that 1.3's make much for power until they wind up.  <P>Nick, you probably know them, I see both of those cars fairly often.  Like I said, the guy with the Prelude was cool, but the RX7 guy seemed a little aloof.  I've heard from a couple people that he thinks his car is GOD.  I spose I could have heard wrong.||||reg||1
