Z||000016||danny boy||03-23-2001||10:03 PM||||no way, man.my car is twinturbo and I might as well get out and push till I get spooled. Everytime I pull alongside an F body or a Mustang they think they have me till I get to 2700 RPM or so. Then its goodnite Irene. Hehe, Turbos are great.Wonder if my stock turbos will work on the GT?Hmmm....<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||03-23-2001||11:19 PM||||It all depends on the type of turbo setup. My friend who runs a Pete farell Rx7 in the one lap of america , dumped the twin turbo , for a single unit. I know 300ZX TT's use 2 T25 (I beliece) turbo's Where as a supra uses a sequential turbo system that uses a smaller turbo for low speeds and quick response , then switches to the bigger for higher end. The same idea can be seen on a Lexus GS300 , it uses 2 seperate intake runners , one for low end TQ , the other for upper end power...neat setup , <P><BR>JM<BR>Former Lexus salesperson<BR>Former Nissan Repo man<BR>Former Soldier in the generals army (GM)<BR>Even worked for Suzuki (eww)||||reg||1
