Z||000023||filthyscarecrow||03-25-2001||07:18 PM||||when i did the touring thing at road america i raced a 944 up the hill coming off of turn 5. the thing that people who have tons of money don't understand is that if my car accelerates 80% as well as his, and i come off the corner 10 mph faster, i'm going to win. he found that one out the hard way. so did the guy in the corvette. i have a pic of me coming up on his gearbox in turn 6 the same lap that i passed him on the exit of the carousel. sure he kicked my a$$ shut on the following straight, but how much did he pay for his car and he still got passed unwillingly? that was before i went to skip barber, now i'm even faster. i think my friend brad got a picture of the corvette drivers face as we blew past him coming out of the corner. i also wasted a BMW 750 on the hill on the front straight. same strategy- lots of exit speed. i had a few people come up to me afterwards and tell me it was pretty impressive. the only thing i can think of that sucked was the third lap i came into turn 5 and depressed the brakes and not a whole lot happened. brad was flabbergasted by the way i said it. it was total deadpan "um, yeah, i've got the brake pedal to the floor right now. not much is happening. let's try the gears..." i drove the next 2 laps totally without the brakes (just heel-toe downshifting) and i was still right behind the corvette the whole time. that was the best $75 i've ever spent. the best $2200 was for skippy's 3 day school... i can't wait to get into the SAE formula car when we get it built. <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
